From cb4dab32c260a74c75aad74c7753d7bc049cb309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:04:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(tui_gateway): start a prompt turn without taking
 history_lock under _sessions_lock

C14 (multiclient session model e2e) wedged the backend: a session.resume
racing its session's own prompt.submit deadlocked, and every later
create/resume queued behind the stuck _sessions_lock (seed 11 resume hung
60 s, seeds 23/37 could not create a session).

py-spy dumps of two locally reproduced wedges show the same cycle:
- prompt worker: _run_admitted_prompt holds _sessions_lock (close-race
  check + spawn) -> _start_session_work -> start_work waits on the
  session's history_lock to retain the turn admission (added with the
  cross-process admission fence);
- session.resume: _live_session_payload holds history_lock ->
  _rebind_live_transport -> _cancel_ws_orphan_reap waits on _sessions_lock.

Lock order is history_lock -> _sessions_lock (resume, activate and the lazy
reattach all rebind that way). start_work is split into prepare_work
(retains admission under history_lock) and PreparedWork.start (spawn only);
_run_admitted_prompt prepares before _sessions_lock, keeps the _closing
check + spawn atomic under it, and cancels/aborts the prepared work after
releasing it. Other start_work callers are unchanged.

Tests: test_prompt_start_lock_order.py (lock-order invariant and a forced
resume/submit race, both red on the old code; refused-turn admission
give-back).
